WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:36.990
All around the world, there's a movement to be like Sonic and live however you like.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.110
Freedom!

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.320
Freedom!

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.450
Freedom!

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.830
The Freedom Movement is the latest craze.

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:38.780
Freedom!

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.320
Freedom!

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:40.950
Freedom!

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.120
Freedom!

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.830
Due to Sonic's influence, many new world records have been established.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:52.250
The number of world records made this year is also a new world record.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.670
8.5 seconds!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.260
I did it! It's a new record!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.290
Episode 49

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.290
The Day the Earth Stood Still

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.560
That's incredible, Chris.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:13.070
Yeah, but it's not just me. Danny and Francis also made new records.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.610
Sonic's influence is incredible.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.030
Anyway, Sonic is still number one.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.660
Listen, Chris. Sonic is so rude.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.120
He hasn't stopped by even once since I started working.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.750
He shouldn't be that carefree!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.000
You know what I mean, right?

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.920
I do. However...

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.510
I'm jealous of Sonic.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.640
If I wasn't a kid, I want to live like Sonic.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.270
It's nice to be Sonic.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.810
Freedom!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:56.110
We're no longer wanted by the authorities, and we'll officially be free after we finish this volunteer work.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:02.030
I never thought peace would be so wonderful. This is another form of freedom.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.200
I'm home, Decoe and Bocoe!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.620
Welcome home, Chris.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.710
Both Mr. and Mrs. Thorndike are here.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.040
Really?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.290
They're eagerly waiting for you.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.500
Thank you!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.460
He's just a kid when he acts like that.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.340
It must be nice to have a family.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.350
Let's ask Mr. Tanaka and Ms. Topaz to adopt us when they get married.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.900
It's ready.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.780
Dr. Eggman, I can't eat this!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.070
I'll get sick if I eat this.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.030
Don't be so picky!

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:46.950
I've never cooked before in my life.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.790
Let's bring Decoe and Bocoe back.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.130
At this rate, we'll both die from malnutrition!

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:59.550
Stop complaining! I'm relieved that those pests are gone!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.550
This is freedom!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.060
You two are great cooks.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.400
If Ella says so, it must be true.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.070
Umm...

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.900
Many of my employees were skipping work because of the Freedom Movement.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:27.120
Therefore, I decided to give them all a month-long vacation.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.330
It was the right choice, Dad.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.750
It's been a year since the entire family was together for dinner.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.590
I also decided not to do my next movie. That means we're...

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.590
Freedom!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.760
Exactly.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.720
I bought T-shirts for everyone, so you should try them on later.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.260
You're so easily influenced.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.350
Mr. Thorndike.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:53.230
There's a phone call for you.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.730
Okay.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.650
What did you say?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.070
I understand. It's tonight.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.990
I'll be waiting.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.490
Goodbye, Mr. President.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:26.130
More drivers are speeding, claiming that it's their freedom.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:29.350
However, none of them can satisfy me.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.560
You're the one exception.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.520
A sonic boom?

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:43.860
I feel nostalgic, as if it took place ten years ago.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.950
He's small-time.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.490
I'm the S-team leader known as the Irresponsible Man of The Freeway.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:56.040
If you don't have the confidence to outrun me, then stop the car!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.580
What a punk.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.380
That idiot!

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.140
Watch out!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:29.860
I told you so.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.390
Sonic!

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:55.010
Long time no see, leader.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.350
I'm not the leader.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.730
I'm the Irresponsible Man of the Freeway.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:05.230
It must be destiny that we crossed paths again. Let's race, Sonic!

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.700
What about me?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.950
You never give up.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.630
I feel bad quickly, but I also get over it quickly.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.170
Go!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.510
You're even faster.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.360
What's my dream for the future?

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:56.200
That's a tough question.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.740
My dream...

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.620
I know!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:11.050
This is the geophysicist Professor Chaco Bankissy.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.840
Just call me Chaco.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.510
My dream for the future.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:22.640
My dream for the future is to be with Sonic forever.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.900
It sounds a bit childish.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.030
What's that?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.000
Sonic!

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.840
I'm Sonic.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:59.600
Sonic the Hedgehog.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.940
That would've been too good to be true.

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.500
Time will die? That's nonsense!

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.710
No, it's possible.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.590
This world and Sonic's world used to be one.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:41.060
For some reason, it split into two different worlds and dimensions.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:46.140
That means each world had a different timeline.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:51.980
The worlds have now reunited, so the timelines are also reuniting.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.490
What's going to happen?

00:09:54.490 --> 00:10:01.280
If we do nothing, the two timelines will interfere with each other and eventually freeze.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.500
In other words, time will die.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.370
However, it will be different than physical death that humans experience.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.960
Make sure you don't make that mistake.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.920
The professor has named it the Time Stagnation Phenomenon.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.470
Time Stag... What?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:27.770
I see. If time stops, there is no past or future. Physical death will no longer exist.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.520
That sounds like a fairy tale!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:39.150
The rash of world records and the rise of the Freedom Movement prove that the Time Stagnation Phenomenon is occurring.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:45.240
That's why we've come to ask you if it's possible to split the worlds again.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.500
Cause another Chaos Control to happen?

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:53.630
They want to return the world to a time before Sonic and you arrived.

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.700
What did you say?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.620
Chris!

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.080
Chris, listen!

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.500
You're lying, right?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.630
Why would you say that?

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.050
Sonic and I will be apart?

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:48.270
I just want to be with Sonic.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.060
I was able to do those things because Sonic was here.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.440
Because Sonic was here.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.230
Because I want to be with Sonic!

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.780
You're lying! Sonic and I won't be apart!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.990
You're lying!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.870
It's not a lie. Listen, Chris.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.000
If there's a beginning, there's an end.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.830
And it's now time for the end.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.460
You're lying!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.300
Father.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.550
I know. It has to be Eggman.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.640
He's doing something evil again.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:28.560
Yeah, Father. Chris must be right.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.350
I'm sorry, but it's very unlikely.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.100
Chris.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.600
Listen to what I'm about to say.

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:39.520
Chris, you have to think for yourself. We still have time.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.110
I don't want to listen!

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.320
I don't!

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.780
Chris!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.410
What should we do, Chuck?

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.210
I understand how Chris feels.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:59.960
I feel the same as him.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:04.340
I'm old. I don't know how much longer I'll live.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:09.350
But if time freezes, I won't have to worry about that anymore.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:14.940
Maybe you and I can do various experiments forever.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.770
On the other hand...

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:23.030
Can that really be done if there is no future?

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:27.280
That's what I was thinking about.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:31.160
Nothing is forever.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.790
Just like this vase.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:39.000
That's what we believe in when we live.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.550
I had a good time, Tails.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.720
Eggman's doing this. Eggman is the bad guy!

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.560
Chris!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.570
I've looked everywhere for you.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.530
What's wrong? Why are you in a hurry?

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.820
I have a favor to ask.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.450
Please take me to Eggman!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.580
Don't yell that out loud!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.500
They can hear you.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.630
I see.

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:31.260
I understand, but we don't know where Eggman is.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.890
I see.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.980
Everyone must be worried. Let's go home together.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.270
No! I'm going to find him all by myself!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.320
Don't say that. You're putting us in a bad situation.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:47.030
If I don't hurry, Sonic and I will...

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.740
This seems to be a complicated situation.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.120
That guy might be with him.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.620
Chris, wait a moment.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:01.920
Decoe!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.090
Bocoe!

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.340
Cross!

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.350
And then...

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:30.860
You called for me? Bokkun is here!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.660
Oh, it's the traitors.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.870
Messenger Robo, take me to Eggman!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.080
I said my name was Bokkun! Now I definitely won't!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.050
You idiot.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.880
I'm so hungry that I can't fly.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.090
You must be having a hard time.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.680
It's all your fault!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:59.100
Thanks to you, I haven't eaten anything decent!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.890
We have lots of food!

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.060
And high-grade oil.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.520
Okay. I'll tell you where he is.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.320
I'm sorry, Mr. Thorndike.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.370
I had no idea. I'm very sorry!

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.410
Don't worry about it. It's not your fault.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.210
As his parents, we should've been more sympathetic.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.840
Seeing him like that...

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.050
Can't we do anything?

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.090
Let's call the President immediately.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.890
We'll have GUN and the police search for him.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.350
Please do that.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.850
Don't get carried away!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.230
Father, you know where he is?

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.650
He's going to see Eggman.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.360
What?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.490
He's your son.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.910
Let's trust him.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:17:01.450
Chris knows that learning the truth may be painful, but he still left to look for answers.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:09.130
Eggman!

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.930
Decoe! Bocoe!

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:25.310
Do you think I'll let you come back after you betrayed me?

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.770
Eggman!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:30.860
Well done, you two. You brought me a hostage as a gift.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:34.190
That's why you're Dr. Eggman's minions.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.820
You're wrong. I asked them to bring me here.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:38.990
What?

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:43.120
Tell me what you're planning to do!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.830
Me?

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:51.960
Does Sonic bother you that much? I just want to be with him!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.970
I see.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.440
You're right, Chris.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:15.990
This is the evil genius Dr. Eggman's final plan to create the Eggman Empire!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.030
I'm impressed that you found out.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.790
I won't let you do it, Eggman!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.330
Turn this world's time back to what it was!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.000
What can one kid do?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.670
You'll probably end up crying and asking for Sonic.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:34.710
What?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.380
Don't resort to violence!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.680
Let him go. He can't do anything anyway.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:45.520
Whenever anything happens, he quickly blames someone else.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.190
Stop acting like a spoiled child!

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:53.480
I have nothing to do with it this time!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.070
Too bad.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:04.030
You're lying.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.200
Everyone is lying to me!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.960
It's not a lie.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.790
Yes, it is!

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:17.630
How long are you going to act like a spoiled child, you fool!

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:24.720
Since you and Sonic always interfered with my plans together, I thought you were a little tougher.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.390
I was wrong.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:32.270
You always rely on others and blame other people.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:36.070
If you think you can get away with that forever, you're wrong!

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.530
You only want to be with Sonic?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.740
